<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Waigel-verbal text of budget pact agreed by all.</title>
<headline>Waigel-verbal text of budget pact agreed by all.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Friday that the verbal text of a proposed stability pact to ensure fiscal discipline in monetary union had been agreed by all 15 European Union member states.</p>
<p>&quot;We have agreed on a text which defines the exceptional circumstances (in which a budget deficit may be exceeded without penalty),&quot; Waigel said. &quot;We have still to decide on precise figures, but we are no longer far apart,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>He stressed that the proposed text offered a clear definition of the exceptional circumstances.</p>
</text>
